            <!-- PHASE 2: BRONZE -->
            <section class="doc-section" data-aos="fade-up">
                <div class="doc-title">
                    <i class="fas fa-database"></i>
                    <h2>Phase 1: Bronze Layer (Data Ingestion)</h2>
                </div>
                <div class="doc-text">
                    <p>An ingestion engine (<em>Stored Procedure</em>: <code>load_bronze</code>) focused on massive performance was developed. It implements a <code>BULK INSERT</code> method under the Full Load standard. An Idempotent pattern for safe restarts (<code>TRUNCATE</code> before inserting) and a <code>TRY...CATCH</code> audit block for error traceability were applied.</p>
                </div>

                <div class="code-window">
                    <div class="code-header">
                        <div class="code-dots"><div class="dot r"></div><div class="dot y"></div><div class="dot g"></div></div>
                        proc_load_bronze.sql (Idempotent Snippet)
                    </div>
                    <div class="code-body">
<span class="sql-keyword">BEGIN TRY</span>
    <span class="sql-keyword">SET</span> @start_time = <span class="sql-func">GETDATE</span>();
    <span class="sql-keyword">TRUNCATE TABLE</span> bronze.crm_sales_details;
    
    <span class="sql-keyword">BULK INSERT</span> bronze.crm_sales_details
    <span class="sql-keyword">FROM</span> <span class="sql-string">'C:\SQL_Datasets\source_crm\sales_details.csv'</span>
    <span class="sql-keyword">WITH</span> (
        FIRSTROW = 2,
        FIELDTERMINATOR = <span class="sql-string">','</span>,
        TABLOCK <span class="sql-comment">-- Table-level write performance optimization</span>
    );
    
    <span class="sql-keyword">SET</span> @end_time = <span class="sql-func">GETDATE</span>();
    <span class="sql-keyword">PRINT</span> <span class="sql-string">'>> Load Duration: '</span> + <span class="sql-func">CAST</span>(<span class="sql-func">DATEDIFF</span>(second, @start_time, @end_time) <span class="sql-keyword">AS</span> <span class="sql-keyword">NVARCHAR</span>) + <span class="sql-string">' sec'</span>;
<span class="sql-keyword">END TRY</span>
<span class="sql-keyword">BEGIN CATCH</span>
    <span class="sql-keyword">PRINT</span> <span class="sql-string">'ERROR OCCURRED: '</span> + <span class="sql-func">ERROR_MESSAGE</span>();
<span class="sql-keyword">END CATCH</span>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </section>

            <!-- PHASE 3: SILVER -->
            <section class="doc-section" data-aos="fade-up">
                <div class="doc-title">
                    <i class="fas fa-filter"></i>
                    <h2>Phase 2: Silver Layer (Cleansing & QA)</h2>
                </div>
                <div class="doc-text">
                    <p>Business data transformation (<em>Data Cleansing</em>) is executed in this layer. The goal is to prepare data for analysis by performing rigorous mathematical validations, null resolution, column standardization (e.g., gender, country), and historical date normalization applying <strong>Window Functions</strong> to generate non-overlapping intervals.</p>
                </div>

                <div class="code-window">
                    <div class="code-header">
                        <div class="code-dots"><div class="dot r"></div><div class="dot y"></div><div class="dot g"></div></div>
                        proc_load_silver.sql (Advanced Transformation)
                    </div>
                    <div class="code-body">
<span class="sql-keyword">SELECT</span>
    <span class="sql-comment">-- 1. Extraction of hidden Foreign Keys in text strings</span>
    <span class="sql-func">REPLACE</span>(<span class="sql-func">SUBSTRING</span>(prd_key, 1, 5), <span class="sql-string">'-'</span>, <span class="sql-string">'_'</span>) <span class="sql-keyword">AS</span> cat_id,
    
    <span class="sql-comment">-- 2. Handling missing values and nulls</span>
    <span class="sql-func">ISNULL</span>(prd_cost, 0) <span class="sql-keyword">AS</span> prd_cost,
    
    <span class="sql-comment">-- 3. Window Function (LEAD) for slowly changing dimensions (SCD2)</span>
    <span class="sql-func">CAST</span>(
        <span class="sql-func">LEAD</span>(prd_start_dt) <span class="sql-keyword">OVER</span> (<span class="sql-keyword">PARTITION BY</span> prd_key <span class="sql-keyword">ORDER BY</span> prd_start_dt) - 1 
        <span class="sql-keyword">AS DATE</span>
    ) <span class="sql-keyword">AS</span> prd_end_dt
<span class="sql-keyword">FROM</span> bronze.crm_prd_info;
                    </div>
                </div>

                <h3 style="color: white; margin-bottom: 1rem; font-size: 1.2rem;">Test Suite (Data Quality Assurance)</h3>
                <ul class="qa-list">
                    <li class="qa-item">
                        <i class="fas fa-shield-alt"></i>
                        <div><strong>Mathematical & Entity Integrity</strong>Strict validation of <code>sales = quantity * price</code>. Correction of negative prices and prevention of division by zero using <code>NULLIF</code>. Primary keys integrity check.</div>
                    </li>
                    <li class="qa-item">
                        <i class="fas fa-shield-alt"></i>
                        <div><strong>Chronological Anomalies</strong>Blocking shipping dates prior to order dates, exclusion of unrealistic birth dates, and <code>prd_start_dt &lt; prd_end_dt</code> range validation.</div>
                    </li>
                    <li class="qa-item">
                        <i class="fas fa-shield-alt"></i>
                        <div><strong>Data Governance & Metadata</strong>Injection of the mandatory audit column (e.g., <code>dwh_create_date</code>) to ensure traceability of the exact load millisecond into the Data Warehouse.</div>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </section>

            <!-- PHASE 4: GOLD -->
            <section class="doc-section" style="border-color: var(--primary);" data-aos="fade-up">
                <div class="doc-title">
                    <i class="fas fa-star" style="color: #ffbd2e;"></i>
                    <h2 style="color: var(--primary);">Phase 3: Gold Layer (Dimensional Modeling)</h2>
                </div>
                <div class="doc-text">
                    <p>The final analytical layer (Sales Data Mart) was built using <strong>Analytical Views</strong>, establishing a pure <strong>Star Schema</strong>. Normalized dimensions were integrated generating dynamic <strong>Surrogate Keys</strong> to decouple the Data Warehouse from changes in the source systems. Centralized sales metrics connect with normalized dimensions through One-to-Many relationships.</p>
                </div>
                
                <div class="arch-grid" style="grid-template-columns: 1fr;">
                    <div class="arch-img-card" style="max-width: 800px; margin: 0 auto; background: rgba(0, 10, 30, 0.8);">
                        <img src="data_model.jpg" alt="Sales Data Mart - Star Schema" onclick="if(this.requestFullscreen) this.requestFullscreen();">
                        <h4>Dimensional Model (Data Mart)</h4>
                        <p>Final Entity-Relationship design implemented in the Gold Layer: <code>fact_sales</code> joined via <em>Foreign Keys</em> to <code>dim_customers</code> and <code>dim_products</code>. Includes calculations like <em>Sales = Quantity * price</em> and standardization of descriptive columns.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="code-window">
                    <div class="code-header">
                        <div class="code-dots"><div class="dot r"></div><div class="dot y"></div><div class="dot g"></div></div>
                        ddl_gold.sql (Surrogate Keys Generation)
                    </div>
                    <div class="code-body">
<span class="sql-keyword">CREATE VIEW</span> gold.dim_customers <span class="sql-keyword">AS</span>
<span class="sql-keyword">SELECT</span>
    <span class="sql-comment">-- Dynamic Surrogate Key generation for analytical model isolation</span>
    <span class="sql-func">ROW_NUMBER</span>() <span class="sql-keyword">OVER</span> (<span class="sql-keyword">ORDER BY</span> cst_id) <span class="sql-keyword">AS</span> customer_key, 
    
    ci.cst_firstname <span class="sql-keyword">AS</span> first_name,
    la.cntry         <span class="sql-keyword">AS</span> country,
    
    <span class="sql-comment">-- Data Integration (Conflict resolution between CRM vs ERP sources)</span>
    <span class="sql-keyword">CASE</span> 
        <span class="sql-keyword">WHEN</span> ci.cst_gndr != <span class="sql-string">'n/a'</span> <span class="sql-keyword">THEN</span> ci.cst_gndr <span class="sql-comment">-- Business Rule: CRM is the master</span>
        <span class="sql-keyword">ELSE</span> <span class="sql-func">COALESCE</span>(ca.gen, <span class="sql-string">'n/a'</span>)               <span class="sql-comment">-- Fallback: ERP as secondary source</span>
    <span class="sql-keyword">END</span> <span class="sql-keyword">AS</span> gender
<span class="sql-keyword">FROM</span> silver.crm_cust_info ci
<span class="sql-keyword">LEFT JOIN</span> silver.erp_cust_az12 ca <span class="sql-keyword">ON</span> ci.cst_key = ca.cid;
                    </div>
                </div>
            </section>

            <!-- PHASE 5: EDA -->
            <section class="doc-section" data-aos="fade-up">
                <div class="doc-title">
                    <i class="fas fa-chart-line"></i>
                    <h2>Phase 4: Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA)</h2>
                </div>
                <div class="doc-text">
                    <p>After modeling the <em>Data Warehouse</em>, an Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA) process was executed to interrogate the Gold Layer using T-SQL. Through cross-segmentations and aggregations between Dimensions and Measures, critical business trends and actionable <em>Insights</em> were discovered.</p>
                </div>

                <div class="code-window">
                    <div class="code-header">
                        <div class="code-dots"><div class="dot r"></div><div class="dot y"></div><div class="dot g"></div></div>
                        eda_analysis.sql (Sales Ranking with Window Functions)
                    </div>
                    <div class="code-body">
<span class="sql-comment">-- Report: Identify the top 5 most profitable products historically</span>
<span class="sql-keyword">SELECT</span> * <span class="sql-keyword">FROM</span> (
    <span class="sql-keyword">SELECT</span> 
        p.product_name,
        <span class="sql-func">SUM</span>(f.sales_amount) <span class="sql-keyword">AS</span> total_revenue,
        <span class="sql-func">RANK</span>() <span class="sql-keyword">OVER</span> (<span class="sql-keyword">ORDER BY</span> <span class="sql-func">SUM</span>(f.sales_amount) <span class="sql-keyword">DESC</span>) <span class="sql-keyword">AS</span> sales_rank
    <span class="sql-keyword">FROM</span> gold.fact_sales f
    <span class="sql-keyword">LEFT JOIN</span> gold.dim_products p 
        <span class="sql-keyword">ON</span> f.product_key = p.product_key
    <span class="sql-keyword">GROUP BY</span> p.product_name
) ranking_query
<span class="sql-keyword">WHERE</span> sales_rank <= 5;
                    </div>
                </div>

                <h3 style="color: white; margin-bottom: 1rem; font-size: 1.2rem;">Key Analytical Insights:</h3>
                <ul class="qa-list">
                    <li class="qa-item">
                        <i class="fas fa-chart-pie" style="color: var(--primary);"></i>
                        <div><strong>Proportion and Magnitude Analysis</strong>Grouping of Measures (Sales) by Dimension (Category). The "Bikes" category generated a volume of $28 Million, representing the core profitability pillar of the business.</div>
                    </li>
                    <li class="qa-item">
                        <i class="fas fa-trophy" style="color: var(--primary);"></i>
                        <div><strong>Ranking and Segmentation (Top Spenders)</strong>Identification of the most valuable customers using a combined approach of grouping functions and subqueries, delivering an actionable list for the loyalty department.</div>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </section>

        </div>
